  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/thepianistdirector/grid-horizons/zipball/v1.0.0rc4",
  "body": "Grid Horizons 1.0 RC4 is an offline simulation laboratory for a declared synthetic radial distribution feeder. It supports baseline and bounded storage/tap comparisons, independent residual and energy checks, sensitivity campaigns, an accessible HTML workbench, and study export/import with failure recovery.\n\nStart with the complete ZIP or the install-free Python zipapp. Tested environment: Linux x86_64, CPython 3.12.14; no runtime pip dependencies or private credentials. The complete archive includes source, examples, documentation, raw results, screenshots and three reproducible study packages.\n\nThree bounded findings:\n- Solver convergence alone did not establish numerical validity; loose-tolerance cases failed independent residual checks.\n- Storage reduced peak import in the tested feasible confirmation cases while increasing total energy loss by 2.01\u20132.37 kWh/day.\n- Nominal schedule benefits and feasibility did not persist across every predeclared timing/current stress.\n\nValidation: 75 runtime tests, 34 plan tests, 22 clean-package CLI checks, 22 browser assertions, and standalone replay of 153 scenarios with all 715 policy records byte-identical. A separate Astra agent performed skeptical reproduction. These are computational checks on the same host; external human first-use and qualified model review remain pending. This is a prerelease, with no field-control, certification, peer-review or broad physical-validity claim.\n\nPackaging revision 2 is the exact owner-approved candidate. It repairs dependencies in the separate study archives without changing RC4 application bytes or numerical results. Verify downloads with SHA256SUMS. ASSETS.json and REVIEW.md are preserved prepublication review records; their historical pending-publication language is superseded by this release page and current repository status.\n\nApplication SHA-256: `15aaa7913e4069b9483fcb721032c812a8babc865968d652bb681f031abc7c6e`\n\nComplete ZIP SHA-256: `1c90022a5fb981397288a54e0c75b2a7bd952065ec8d37ce85cb2e0093358c24`\n\n[First-run guide and source](https://github.com/thepianistdirector/grid-horizons#readme) \u00b7 [Findings and reports](https://github.com/thepianistdirector/grid-horizons/tree/main/research) \u00b7 [Tanduna project](https://tanduna.com/projects/grid-horizons)\n\nThe prepared 255-task/31-wave Tanduna plan is an export. Native submission/publication requires authenticated reconciliation and platform governance and is not asserted by this release. See REVIEW-INSTRUCTIONS.md for the concrete external first-use and qualified review workflow.\n"
